==Finnish==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|fi|lang1=urj-fin-pro|*louna|as}}, from {{der|fi|urj-fpr-pro|*lowna||day, midday}}. Cognates include {{cog|krl|lounat||evening/main meal}}, {{cog|vep|louna}}, {{cog|vot|lõunõ||south, lunch}}, {{cog|et|lõuna||south, lunch}} and {{cog|koi|лун}}. Permic cognates have the meaning "day", whereas Baltic-Finnic cognates denote the direction where the Sun is at midday or the meal eaten at midday.

The compass point meaning was clarified in the 19th century; in earlier text and dialects ''lounas'' may mean either south, southwest or southeast. Compare {{m|fi|lounatuuli||southern wind}}. <ref>{{R:Hakkinen 2004}}</ref>

